---
import { getRelativeLocaleUrl } from 'astro:i18n'
import type { Locale } from '@/lib/site'
import type { RedactionData } from '@/lib/redaction/types'
import data from '@/data/redaction/latest.json'

interface Props { locale: Locale }
const { locale } = Astro.props
const de = locale === 'de'
const d = data as unknown as RedactionData
const workUrl = getRelativeLocaleUrl(locale, '/redaction')

const txt = {
  h1: de ? 'Methodenblatt — Editorial Deadline' : 'Method sheet — Editorial Deadline',
  revealHead: de ? 'Worum es geht' : 'What this is',
  reveal: de
    ? 'Das öffentliche Protokoll wird nicht nur geschrieben, sondern auch entschrieben. Veröffentlichung macht Schlagzeilen; das spätere Verschwinden nicht. Dieses Instrument zählt das Weggenommene — den durchgestrichenen Text — und macht jeden Fund über zwei Archiv-Permalinks überprüfbar. Reinste „Dark Data": Daten, die ein System zurücknimmt.'
    : 'The public record is not only written but un-written. Publication makes headlines; the later disappearance does not. This instrument counts the thing taken away — the struck-through text — and makes every finding checkable via two archive permalinks. The purest "dark data": data a system takes back.',
  s1: de ? '1. Quellen & Lizenzen' : '1. Sources & licences',
  s1body: de
    ? `Internet Archive — Wayback Machine, über die CDX-API (${d.source.license}, frei, keine Auth). Beobachtet wird eine kuratierte, versionierte Liste offizieller Seiten; jeder Fund ist archiv-belegt (Statuscode + archivierte Fassungen), nie eine Live-Abfrage — darum reproduzierbar.`
    : `Internet Archive — Wayback Machine, via the CDX API (${d.source.license}, free, no auth). It watches a curated, versioned list of official pages; every finding is archive-sourced (status code + archived versions), never a live fetch — hence reproducible.`,
  s2: de ? '2. Kadenz' : '2. Cadence',
  s2body: de
    ? 'Täglich. Die Maschine wählt selbst: die substanziellste Schwärzung des Tages (Salienz × entferntes Volumen). An stillen Tagen vermerkt sie, dass das Archiv nichts zurückgenommen hat — Stille ist eine Aussage, keine Lücke. Kanonisches Artefakt: versionierte JSON in src/data/redaction/ — Git ist das Archiv.'
    : 'Daily. The machine selects on its own: the most substantive redaction of the day (salience × removed volume). On quiet days it notes that the archive took nothing back — silence is a statement, not a gap. Canonical artefact: versioned JSON in src/data/redaction/ — git is the archive.',
  s3: de ? '3. Verarbeitung' : '3. Processing',
  s3body: de
    ? 'Pro URL: CDX-Captures holen (collapse=digest) → Löschungs-Kandidat (Statuscode 200→4xx) oder Inhalts-Entfernung (Digest-Wechsel der beiden jüngsten 200-Captures) → Gültigkeitsgate vor jedem Diff → beide Fassungen roh ziehen, Haupttext extrahieren, auf Satzebene diffen → entfernte Passagen + Token zählen. Hinzufügungen werden nicht gewertet (Schwärzen = Wegnehmen).'
    : 'Per URL: fetch CDX captures (collapse=digest) → deletion candidate (status 200→4xx) or content removal (digest change between the two newest 200-captures) → validity gate before any diff → pull both versions raw, extract main text, diff at sentence level → count removed passages + tokens. Additions are not scored (redaction = taking away).',
  gateHead: de
    ? 'Gültigkeitsgate & nachgeprüfte Löschungen (v3)'
    : 'The validity gate & checked deletions (v3)',
  gateBody: de
    ? 'Eine Capture zählt nur als Seitenfassung, wenn sie (a) Status 200 trägt, (b) mindestens 40 Tokens Haupttext liefert, (c) keinen Challenge-Fingerabdruck zeigt („Verifying your browser", „Incident ID", „Attention Required", „Just a moment", „Checking your browser" — benannte, versionierte Liste, VALIDITY_VERSION) und (d) nicht überwiegend Consent-/Cookie-Text oder eine reine Navigationsliste ist. Alles andere ist `unverifiable`: gezählt, ausgewiesen, nie gediffed. Und ein 4xx auf der jüngsten Capture ist nur ein Löschungs-Kandidat: bevor „Löschung" im Record steht, wird die Live-URL geprüft — live 404/410 bestätigt, live 200 widerlegt (Archivfehler), 403/429 oder eine Challenge-Seite sind Bot-Wall, 451 wird getrennt geführt. Anlass: das Memory-Hole-Audit vom 2026-08-14 reproduzierte beide Falsch-Positiven.'
    : 'A capture counts as a page version only if it (a) carries status 200, (b) yields at least 40 tokens of main text, (c) shows no challenge fingerprint ("Verifying your browser", "Incident ID", "Attention Required", "Just a moment", "Checking your browser" — a named, versioned list, VALIDITY_VERSION) and (d) is not predominantly consent/cookie text or a pure navigation pile. Everything else is `unverifiable`: counted, disclosed, never diffed. And a 4xx on the newest capture is only a deletion candidate: before the word "deletion" enters the record the live URL is rechecked — live 404/410 confirms, live 200 refutes it (an archive error), 403/429 or a challenge page is a bot-wall, 451 is reported apart. Occasion: the memory-hole audit of 2026-08-14 reproduced both false positives.',
  aiHead: de ? 'KI/ML — symbolisch, auditierbar' : 'AI/ML — symbolic, auditable',
  aiBody: de
    ? 'Das Lab experimentiert mit Daten UND KI; symbolische KI ist hier die Wahl, weil prüfbar. Die Salienz ist ein offengelegtes Regelwerk (versioniert): trägt der entfernte Text Zahlen, Daten, Eigennamen, Verneinungen oder Verpflichtungsverben („wird", „muss", „verpflichtet"), gilt er als substanziell; nur Markup/Whitespace ist kosmetisch (Score 0) und kann die Tagesschwärzung nie gewinnen. Kein LLM in v1. Optional/künftig: ein gegen den Diff verifizierter LLM-Klassifikator der Entfernungs-Art (Prompt offengelegt).'
    : 'The lab experiments with data AND AI; symbolic AI is the choice here because it is checkable. Salience is a disclosed rule set (versioned): if the removed text carries numbers, dates, named entities, negations or commitment verbs ("will", "must", "pledge"), it counts as substantive; markup/whitespace only is cosmetic (score 0) and can never win the redaction of the day. No LLM in v1. Optional/future: an LLM classifier of the removal kind, verified against the diff (prompt disclosed).',
  s4: de ? '4. Grenzen der Methode' : '4. Limits of the method',
  s4items: de
    ? [
        'Umschreibung ist nicht Vertuschung — das Instrument behauptet keine Absicht; legitime Korrekturen werden nicht von Unterdrückung unterschieden.',
        'Die Seed-Liste ist eine redaktionelle Wahl; gemessen wird, was beobachtet wird, nicht „das Internet".',
        'Wayback-Erfassungsbias: gemessen wird gegen verfügbare Captures; was nie erfasst wurde, bleibt unsichtbar.',
        'Die Haupttext-Extraktion ist heuristisch (Version offengelegt) und kann Inhalt verfehlen oder fehl-segmentieren.',
        'Die Salienz-Regeln und -Gewichte sind eine gesetzte, offengelegte Wahl (SALIENCE_VERSION).',
        'Das Gültigkeitsgate ist bewusst streng: eine echte, aber sehr kurze Seite fällt als `unverifiable` heraus. Lieber ein verschwiegener Fund als ein erfundener — die Zahl steht auf der Seite.',
        'Die Live-Nachprüfung ist der einzige Nicht-Archiv-Abruf: Sie entscheidet nur über „gelöscht ja/nein" und wird nie als Beleg zitiert; belegt wird weiter mit Archiv-Permalinks.',
      ]
    : [
        'Rewriting is not cover-up — the instrument claims no intent; legitimate corrections are not distinguished from suppression.',
        'The seed list is an editorial choice; this measures what it watches, not "the internet".',
        'Wayback coverage bias: measured against available captures; what was never captured stays invisible.',
        'Main-text extraction is heuristic (version disclosed) and may miss or mis-segment content.',
        'The salience rules and weights are a set, disclosed choice (SALIENCE_VERSION).',
        'The validity gate is deliberately strict: a genuine but very short page drops out as `unverifiable`. A withheld finding beats an invented one — and the number is on the page.',
        'The live recheck is the only non-archive request: it decides "gone or not", is never cited as evidence, and the evidence stays the two archive permalinks.',
      ],
  s5: de ? '5. Compute-Fußabdruck' : '5. Compute footprint',
  s5body: de
    ? 'Wenige leichte HTTP-Abrufe je beobachteter Seite und Tag, kein API-Key, kein LLM. Die Site selbst ist statisch.'
    : 'A few lightweight HTTP fetches per watched page per day, no API key, no LLM. The site itself is static.',
  s6: de ? '6. Änderungsprotokoll' : '6. Change log',
  s6items: de
    ? [
        'v1 (2026-06) — Erstfassung: CDX-Diff (Löschung + Entfernung), symbolische Salienz, zwei Archiv-Permalinks je Fund.',
        'v2 (2026-08-14) — die World Chamber: GDG-Umschreibungsregister + hauseigene Stichproben-Löschrate (Kammer 2).',
        'v3 (2026-08-15) — Gültigkeitsgate vor jedem Diff und live nachgeprüfte Löschungen; `unverifiable` als ausgewiesene Zahl (Schema v2). Anlass: die zwei im Memory-Hole-Audit reproduzierten Falsch-Positiven.',
        'Was das für die Zeit davor heißt (nachgerechnet 2026-08-22): Die 50 Nächte vor dem Gate tragen 98 Records der Art „Löschung“, 97 davon auf HTTP 403 der jüngsten Aufnahme — genau das Bot-Wall-Muster, das v3 ausschließt — und einer auf 404 ohne Live-Bestätigung. In den Nächten seit v3: keine. Die alten Records bleiben unverändert stehen: das Archiv ist append-only, und ein Werk über das Umschreiben der Vergangenheit schreibt seine eigene nicht um.',
      ]
    : [
        'v1 (2026-06) — first edition: CDX diff (deletion + removal), symbolic salience, two archive permalinks per finding.',
        'v2 (2026-08-14) — the world chamber: GDG rewrite register + in-house sampled deletion rate (chamber 2, above).',
        'v3 (2026-08-15) — validity gate before any diff and live-checked deletions; `unverifiable` as a disclosed number (schema v2). Occasion: the two false positives reproduced in the memory-hole audit.',
        'What that means for everything before it (recounted 2026-08-22): the 50 nights before the gate carry 98 records of kind “deletion”, 97 of them resting on an HTTP 403 on the newest capture — exactly the bot-wall pattern v3 excludes — and one on a 404 that was never confirmed live. Since v3: none. Those records are left standing unchanged, because the archive is append-only and a work about the rewriting of the past does not rewrite its own.',
      ],
  toWork: de ? 'Zum Experiment' : 'To the experiment',
}

// Chamber 2 — English only (the ecology is EN-only; the de branches above are legacy).
const w2 = {
  head: 'Chamber 2 — the world’s press (since 2026-08-14)',
  intro:
    'Deletion is not censorship. Articles vanish for banal reasons — CMS migrations, ' +
    'paywalling, corrections policy, licence clocks on agency copy — and headlines are ' +
    'rewritten for banal reasons too. The chamber counts disappearance and rewriting, ' +
    'shows receipts, and asserts no motive. That sentence stands first on purpose.',
  sources:
    'GDELT Global Difference Graph (gdelt-bq.gdeltv2.gdg_partitioned via BigQuery): every ' +
    'monitored article is recrawled at +24 h and +1 week; yesterday’s UTC partition is ' +
    'read nightly — status counts plus all English-stream title rewrites (page_lang as ' +
    'classified by GDELT; misdetections occur and are visible). The GDG’s current ' +
    'pipeline records no deletion class (verified 2026-08-13/14 — the 2018 deletion rates ' +
    'describe a retired version), so deletion is measured in-house: each night a random ' +
    'sample of 300 articles from the day’s news pool (GDELT GKG 2.1 raw files, hourly ' +
    'stride, seed disclosed as world-sample-<date>) is committed to git; the next night, ' +
    'when its articles are ~29–53 h old, it is rechecked. The committed manifest is the ' +
    'receipt: our own history proves what stood there. Licence: Data — The GDELT ' +
    'Project, cited and linked on every derived file.',
  filter:
    'The triviality filter (FILTER_VERSION v1) is deterministic, rule-based and fully ' +
    'disclosed in code — no model in the loop: normalization (NFC, entities, stray markup), ' +
    'site-name affixes, ellipsis truncations, case/punctuation and function-word-only edits ' +
    'are trivial; rolling-coverage markers (live, highlights, as it happened) and ' +
    'numbers-only diffs are running updates; titles with almost no lexical continuity are ' +
    'counted apart as replaced (page reuse cannot be excluded); the rest are reframings. ' +
    'The register shows at most three, selected by rule (SELECTION_VERSION v1): exchanges ' +
    'in place first (words removed AND added), higher token-set similarity first, ' +
    'capitalized substitutions as actor proxies, one entry per domain, duplicate pairs ' +
    'collapsed, deterministic tie-breaks. MediaSpin (ICWSM 2026) is the academic benchmark ' +
    'this coarser rule set is measured against.',
  limits: [
    'GDELT’s recrawl schedule (+24 h, +1 wk) bounds what "rewritten" means here; the recrawl window of each register entry is shown.',
    'The deletion rate counts 404/410 among decidable answers only. HTTP 451 is reported apart — from a German vantage point it can mean EU geo-blocking rather than takedown; it needs per-domain classification or a second vantage before it may be headlined.',
    'Bot-walls (403/429) and network failures are unverifiable and excluded from the denominator, disclosed as counts. The house’s honest user agent earns more bot-walls than a disguised crawler would — that share is itself published.',
    'A page that answers 200 with different content (soft deletion) counts as reachable: the gone rate is a floor.',
    'Pure word-order reversals ("A attacks B" → "B attacks A") pass the v1 filter as trivial — a named blind spot, on the change-log for v2.',
    'The receipt sample covers the English-monitored GKG stream; the GDG covers more. The gap is a number, not a silence.',
    'Quoted headlines remain the works of their authors and publishers, cited as evidence under quotation right; the house’s CC0 covers its own measurement data, never quoted third-party text.',
    'Restraint rules, disclosed: 451 receipts carry the title only as a SHA-256 hash (the day record does not re-publish what the law removed); a vanished headline matching crime/court markers is withheld on the page (personal-rights caution) while the count stands. Justified erasure requests reach the house via the imprint; affected receipts are redacted case by case — the numbers never change.',
  ],
  cost:
    'Two partition-filtered BigQuery queries per night (≈ 0.1–0.2 GB billed, ≈ ' +
    '3–6 GB/month — well inside the free tier and the 10 €/month guideline); job ' +
    'IDs and bytes billed are committed in every day’s trace. Plus ~24 raw-file ' +
    'downloads for the pool sample and 300 status-only rechecks (no bodies read).',
}
---

<main id="main" class="flex-1">
<div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-14">
  <h1 class="mb-8 text-xl font-semibold">{txt.h1}</h1>

  <section class="mb-10 border border-line bg-panel/60 p-5">
    <h2 class="mb-2 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-fg-faint">{txt.revealHead}</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed">{txt.reveal}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="mb-2 font-semibold">{txt.s1}</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">{txt.s1body}</p>
    <p class="mt-2"><a href={d.source.url} class="font-mono text-xs text-fg-faint transition-colors hover:text-fg" rel="noopener">{d.source.url}</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-2 font-semibold">{txt.s2}</h2><p class="leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">{txt.s2body}</p></section>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="mb-2 font-semibold">{txt.s3}</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">{txt.s3body}</p>
    <p class="mt-2">
      <a href="https://github.com/frankbueltge/frankbueltge.de/tree/main/pipelines/redaction"
        class="font-mono text-xs text-fg-faint transition-colors hover:text-fg" rel="noopener">→ pipelines/redaction</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8 border-l-2 border-accent/60 pl-4">
    <h2 class="mb-2 font-semibold">{txt.gateHead}</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">{txt.gateBody}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8 border-l-2 border-line pl-4">
    <h2 class="mb-2 font-semibold">{txt.aiHead}</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">{txt.aiBody}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="mb-2 font-semibold">{txt.s4}</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-fg-muted">{txt.s4items.map((i) => <li>{i}</li>)}</ul>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-2 font-semibold">{txt.s5}</h2><p class="leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">{txt.s5body}</p></section>

  <section class="mb-10 border-t border-line pt-8">
    <h2 class="mb-3 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-fg-faint">{w2.head}</h2>
    <p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed">{w2.intro}</p>

    <h3 class="mb-2 font-semibold">Sources, receipts &amp; licences</h3>
    <p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">{w2.sources}</p>

    <h3 class="mb-2 font-semibold">The versioned filter &amp; the register's selection rule</h3>
    <p class="mb-2 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">{w2.filter}</p>
    <p class="mb-6">
      <a href="https://github.com/frankbueltge/frankbueltge.de/tree/main/pipelines/redaction/src/redaction/world"
        class="font-mono text-xs text-fg-faint transition-colors hover:text-fg" rel="noopener">→ pipelines/redaction/src/redaction/world</a>
    </p>

    <h3 class="mb-2 font-semibold">Limits of the chamber</h3>
    <ul class="mb-6 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-fg-muted">{w2.limits.map((i) => <li>{i}</li>)}</ul>

    <h3 class="mb-2 font-semibold">Compute footprint &amp; cost</h3>
    <p class="leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">{w2.cost}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="mb-2 font-semibold">{txt.s6}</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-fg-muted">{txt.s6items.map((i) => <li>{i}</li>)}</ul>
  </section>

  <a href={workUrl} class="text-sm text-fg-muted transition-colors hover:text-fg">→ {txt.toWork}</a>
</div>
</main>
